            "text": "The model represents four undistinguished items in each view (upper, right, lower, left) with no identified color or shape. Attention is currently concentrated on the left location in both views; that left item is the most immediately accessible. Other locations in each view have much lower current selection and are less available now.\n\nRecoverability estimates predict how well each item\u2019s information would remain accessible if not revisited: in view A the lower item is the most durable if left unattended, the left and upper items are moderately recoverable, and the right item is least recoverable. In view B the upper and right items are more recoverable than the left and lower items, with the lower item the least durable.\n\nControllability differs by view. In view A issuing a command to select a specific location is predicted to redirect attention reliably to that location, so you can shift access to any of the four items. In view B most command predictions nonetheless return attention to the upper location, so attempts to redirect tend to bring focus back to upper; the view is therefore relatively uncontrollable.",
